  "body": "## Summary / dependency\n\nDepends on #343 (then #340 \u2192 #334 \u2192 #332 \u2192 #331). The user authorized finding or setting up payment staging. This PR adds read-only qualification tooling, not deployment automation or a claim of payment readiness.\n\n- Identify existing API `tdf-hq-studio-audit-staging.fly.dev` and web `tdf-studio-audit-staging-web.fly.dev`; both returned real HTTP 200 health responses.\n- Add a manual opt-in CI job with fixed staging targets, read-only repository permissions, pinned Fly tooling and a sanitized evidence artifact.\n- Project only safe metadata/presence booleans; never print secret values, digests, raw config/error payloads or production app metadata.\n- Final workflow requires separate `FLY_STAGING_API_TOKEN` / `FLY_STAGING_WEB_TOKEN` credentials. No fallback to the shared Fly token. No normal CI gates changed.\n\n## Actual access results\n\nThe existing shared Fly token was exercised inside GitHub Actions and denied both staging apps' config/secret-name reads. Koyeb's configured token returned HTTP 401 to a GET-only app-list request. Evidence: https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/34907233146 (source `2aee92f1bb809d8d0a569a0e535bb10012b7c45a`, report 2026-09-14T23:07:20.546Z).\n\nThe inspection job intentionally failed. These results do not prove token expiry or absent merchant credentials. New per-app staging secret names remain unconfigured; no sandbox account aliases were verified. No hosting setup/deployment, database mutation, provider transaction or production action occurred.\n\n## Tests\n\n- Final local guard suite: `node --test scripts/__tests__/payment-staging-inspection.test.mjs` \u2014 6 passed. Includes exact target restrictions, per-app token isolation/no fallback, projection redaction and GET-only alternative discovery.\n- Workflow YAML syntax parse passed using `YAML.parse_file`; an initial Ruby 2.6 unsupported keyword invocation failed and is documented.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- Prior remote inspector version: 5 guard tests passed; actual hosting qualification failed as above. Final dedicated-token configuration has not authenticated remotely.\n- Recovery/backend/web verification remains in #343; not repeated or misrepresented as sandbox tests here.\n\n## Activation / rollback / risks\n\nAn authorized Fly owner must provide short-lived app-scoped credentials via the existing GitHub secret store, or sign into an authorized local Fly session. Do not send credential values in chat or overwrite production secrets. Rerun the manual inspection before qualifying the dedicated database, migrations, effective sandbox configuration, merchant credentials and callbacks. Keep providers disabled until real sandbox evidence exists.\n\n`docs/payments/staging-access-2026-09-14.md` records exact URLs, commands, hashes/timestamps, results, official sources and the shortest activation path. No migration needed for this tooling. Reverting it only removes inspection; it does not alter runtime services. No screenshots or deployment success are claimed. Draft only; do not merge automatically.\n",
